<description>
Fill unobstructed horizontal gaps between neighboring foreground objects with maroon.

Input structure
- The grid has one connected background color and one foreground color split into several 4-connected solid rectangles.
- Foreground rectangles can be horizontally separated while overlapping in their row spans.
Rule
- For every pair of foreground rectangles with separated column spans and overlapping row spans, consider the rectangle between their bounding boxes.
- Paint that between-box region maroon when no third foreground rectangle has a bounding box crossing both that horizontal gap and the same shared row span.
- Keep all original pixels unchanged.
Key insight
- The bridges are determined by adjacency of object bounding boxes in horizontal layers, not by scanning each row independently.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "black gap regions between horizontally separated 4-connected red rectangular objects",
  "transform": "recolor a gap to maroon across the shared row span of its two red rectangles when no third red bbox crosses both that gap and shared span; preserve all red pixels and other black pixels"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10x10 [observed]
  colors: background BLACK, foreground RED, bridge MAROON (output only)
  rectangles:
    count: 3-5 solid 4-connected RED rectangles
    width: 1-4, height: 2-6, area: 4-18
    no bbox overlap between any pair
    foreground coverage: 27-54% of grid cells [observed]
  bridging_rule:
    for_each_pair: with horizontally separated columns AND overlapping row spans
    bridge: fill the gap rectangle (shared-row-span x column-gap) with MAROON
    blocking: skip if any third rectangle's bbox crosses both the gap columns and the shared row span
    at_least_one_bridge: required (1 or more painted)
  bridge_properties:
    gap_width: 1-5 columns
    row_overlap_height: 1-3 rows
    bridges_per_example: 2-4
    blocked_pairs: 0-1 per example [observed]
  background: BLACK forms exactly 1 connected component (4-conn)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Place 3-5 non-overlapping solid RED rectangles (w 1-4, h 2-6) on a 10x10 BLACK grid
    2. Ensure at least 2 pairs have horizontally-separated columns with overlapping row spans (bridgeable pairs)
    3. Run the solver (pairwise gap-fill with blocking check) to compute bridges
    4. Verify at least 1 bridge is painted and all bridge regions were originally BLACK
    5. The input is the grid before bridge painting; the output includes MAROON bridges
